     "notes": "The pressure reduction is reconstructed as the Fei et al. (2007) Pt Vinet-MGD scale: conventional fcc Z=4 V0=60.38 A^3, K0=277 GPa, K0'=5.08, Tr=300 K, theta0=230 K, gamma0=2.72, q=0.5, n=1, with theta=theta0*(V/V0)^[-gamma(V)]. It is executable as the compatibility-catalog record pt_fcc_fei_2007 but is not a shared .eosmat cross-reference. Exact row-wise recalculation remains impossible because neither the 2016 nor 2022 table publishes Pt volumes. The 300 K application to 199.2 GPa also exceeds Fei et al.'s direct Pt experimental pressure envelope of 0-94 GPa."
